cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below and cite
  the external dataset separately.
title: "Impact-Aware Fraud Prioritization"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Platonov"
    given-names: "Anton"
    affiliation: "Hochschule Bielefeld – University of Applied Sciences and Arts (HSBI)"
version: 0.1.0
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Reproducible software for a budget-conditioned learning-to-rank experiment
  that prioritizes credit-card transactions under limited investigation
  capacity and evaluates Fraud capture separately from Fraud-Amount-proxy
  coverage.
keywords:
  - fraud detection
  - learning to rank
  - credit-card transactions
  - limited investigation capacity
  - reproducible research
